				"79A. Adjudication of penalties.— (1) For the purpose of adjudicating penalties under sections 59, 60, 62, 63, sub-section (1) of section 64, sections 70, 71, 72, 73 and 75, the Metro Railway Administration may appoint an officer managing the functioning of metro station as an adjudicating officer for holding an inquiry and imposing penalties in such manner as may be specified:
			TC
				nan
		TR
			TC

			TC

			TC

			TC
				Provided that the Metro Railway Administration may appoint as many adjudicating officers as may be required.
			TC
				nan
		TR
			TC

			TC

			TC

			TC
				(2) Whoever is aggrieved by an order of the adjudicating officer under sub-section (1) may, within thirty days from the receipt of such order, prefer an appeal to such officer at least one rank higher than the adjudicating officer as may be appointed by the Metro Railway Administration as an appellate authority, in such form and manner as may be specified.
			TC
