			TC
				(2) An appeal may be admitted after the expiry of the period of thirty days if the appellant satisfies the appellate authority that he had sufficient cause for not preferring the appeal within that period.
		TR
			TC

			TC

			TC
				(3) The appellate authority may, after giving the parties to the appeal an opportunity of being heard, pass such order as he may think fit.
		TR
			TC

			TC

			TC
				(4) An appeal under sub-section (1) shall be disposed of within sixty days from the date of filing.
		TR
			TC

			TC

			TC
				33C. Imprisonment for non-payment of
		TR
			TC

			TC

			TC
				penalty.––Where any person fails to pay the penalty imposed under the provisions of this Act and the rules made thereunder within ninety days of such imposition, punishable with imprisonment for a term which may extend to three months or with fine which may extend to twice the amount of the penalty, or with both.
		TR
			TC

			TC

			TC
				he shall be
		TR
			TC

			TC

			TC
				33D. Remittance of penalty.––(1) Where an adjudicating officer imposes a penalty under the provisions of this Act and the rules made thereunder, the amount of the said penalty realised shall be credited to the Fund of the Animal Welfare Board of India constituted under the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals Act, 1960 (59 of 1960).
		TR
			TC

			TC

			TC
				(2) The Board shall utilise the amount realised through penalty for the implementation of the provision of the Act and the rules made thereunder in such manner as may be prescribed by the Central Government.".
